course: dictionary
lesson: 15089
title: Rolled: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The same word can have more than one meaning. Rolled is one of these words. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning fits. «The ball rolled down the hill.» Here rolled is the past form of roll, so the ball moved over and over in the past.
explain: Rolled can also describe something made flat or round by rolling. «She added rolled oats to the pot.» Oats that have been flattened are called rolled oats, so rolled is an adjective here. The clue is the word oats.
explain: In maths and games, rolled can mean a number thrown on dice. «Sam rolled a six and moved six squares.» The words dice and squares are the clues. Always ask: what does the sentence say is happening? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it makes sense.
fact: Rolled is the past tense of roll.
fact: Roll means to move by turning over and over, or to make something flat or round.
fact: «Rolled» can describe something made flat or round, as in «rolled oats» or «dough rolled out».
fact: «Rolled» can mean a number thrown on dice, as in «she rolled a 5».
fact: The words around rolled, such as ball, dice or dough, tell you which meaning fits.
exercise: «The ball rolled across the playground.» What does rolled show? | *The ball moved by turning over and over in the past | The ball was flattened by a bag | The ball was folded into a roll | A number was thrown on dice
exercise: «Mum poured the rolled oats into the pan.» What does rolled mean here? | A number thrown on dice | Moved over and over | *Flattened, as in oats that have been made flat | Wrapped up in paper
exercise: «Tom rolled a 4 and moved four squares.» What does rolled mean here? | Moved over and over on the floor | *A number thrown on dice | Folded up in a roll | Made flat by rolling
test: «The dough was rolled out flat on the table.» What does rolled mean? | *Made flat by rolling | Hidden under a cloth | Fell off the table | A number thrown on dice
test: «Yesterday the coin rolled under the sofa.» Which word shows that this happened in the past? | under | *rolled | sofa | coin
exam: «Ella rolled up her sleeves before the race.» What does rolled mean here? | *Folded or turned up into a roll | Flattened by a heavy weight | A number thrown on dice | A ball moving over and over
